query:
[Bug]: getByRole treats input[type=search] with a broken/non-datalist list attribute as combobox; Chrome computes searchbox

## Version

1.61.1 (also reproduced against `main` @ `4cd8608744bf4d18c9f23578c3cf4a1cd1862b2d`, `packages/injected/src/roleUtils.ts`)

## Steps to reproduce

Save as `repro.js` next to a `node_modules` with `playwright` 1.61.1 (chromium installed), run `node repro.js`:

```js
const { chromium } = require('playwright');

(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();
  const page = await browser.newPage();

  // list="nope" points to nothing: there is no <datalist>, so no suggestion source.
  await page.setContent('<!DOCTYPE html><input type=search list=nope>');
  console.log('combobox  count =', await page.getByRole('combobox').count());   // 1  <-- BUG
  console.log('searchbox count =', await page.getByRole('searchbox').count());  // 0  <-- BUG

  // Same shape with list pointing to a <div> (not a <datalist>): same wrong result.
  await page.setContent('<!DOCTYPE html><input type=search list=dv><div id=dv></div>');
  console.log('combobox  count =', await page.getByRole('combobox').count());   // 1  <-- BUG
  console.log('searchbox count =', await page.getByRole('searchbox').count());  // 0  <-- BUG

  // Control: a real <datalist>. Playwright and Chrome agree on combobox here.
  await page.setContent('<!DOCTYPE html><input type=search list=dl><datalist id=dl></datalist>');
  console.log('combobox  count =', await page.getByRole('combobox').count());   // 1  ok

  await browser.close();
})();
```

Cross-check against the browser's own accessibility tree: open the first snippet in Chrome DevTools,
Elements, Accessibility pane. Chrome computes role **searchbox** for `<input type=search list=nope>`.
Per https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#concept-input-list a `list` attribute that does
not point at a `<datalist>` denotes no suggestion source, and HTML-AAM then maps `input[type=search]`
without a list to `searchbox`.

## Expected behavior

`getByRole('searchbox')` matches the element (and `getByRole('combobox')` does not) whenever the `list`
attribute does not resolve to a `<datalist>`, matching Chrome's computed role and HTML-AAM. Verified via
CDP `Accessibility.getPartialAXTree` on the same DOM node: Chrome 149.0.7827.55 reports `role=searchbox`
for `list=nope`, `list` pointing at a `<div>`, and an empty `list` attribute (3/3 broken-list cases),
and `combobox` only for a real `<datalist>`.

## Actual behavior

Playwright computes `combobox` for all three broken-list cases: `getByRole('combobox')` matches (count 1)
and `getByRole('searchbox')` misses (count 0). `expect(locator).toMatchAriaSnapshot` and role assertions
disagree with what the browser's AX inspector and screen readers report.

## Additional context

Root cause: `packages/injected/src/roleUtils.ts:126` (INPUT implicit-role mapping):

```ts
if (type === 'search')
  return e.hasAttribute('list') ? 'combobox' : 'searchbox';
```

The `search` branch checks `hasAttribute('list')` and nothing else. The next branch (for
`email/tel/text/url`) validates that the IDREF resolves to an actual `<datalist>`:

```ts
if (['email', 'tel', 'text', 'url', ''].includes(type)) {
  // https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#concept-input-list
  const list = getIdRefs(e, e.getAttribute('list'))[0];
  return (list && elementSafeTagName(list) === 'DATALIST') ? 'combobox' : 'textbox';
}
```

Suggested fix: give `search` the same treatment.

```ts
if (type === 'search') {
  const list = getIdRefs(e, e.getAttribute('list'))[0];
  return (list && elementSafeTagName(list) === 'DATALIST') ? 'combobox' : 'searchbox';
}
```

Differential evidence (same DOM node, `roleUtils.ts` bundle @ `4cd8608` vs Chromium AX tree via CDP,
chromium 149.0.7827.55 / playwright 1.61.1): 3/3 broken-list cases diverge (PW `combobox`,
Chrome `searchbox`: nonexistent IDREF, IDREF to a `<div>`, empty `list` attribute); 5/5 controls agree
(real `<datalist>`, no `list`, and the analogous `text`/`email` inputs, which Playwright resolves
through the datalist check above). The `search` branch carries no `SPEC DIFFERENCE` comment, so the
divergence from browser behavior looks unintentional.

## Environment

```
(paste your `npx envinfo --preset playwright` output here before submitting)
Evidence gathered with:
  playwright 1.61.1 (npm), bundled Chromium 149.0.7827.55, headless
  macOS (darwin arm64), Node 24.10.0
  source cross-checked at microsoft/playwright @ 4cd8608744bf4d18c9f23578c3cf4a1cd1862b2d
```

