query:
[CLI]: Screencast showOverlay/showChapter is invisible behind any top-layer element (dialog/popover) — the #39123 fix doesn't cover this path

### What's going on?

**Summary**
page.screencast.showOverlay(html)/showChapter() draw an annotation on top of the live page — used for recording bug-repro screencasts. The annotation is silently hidden whenever the page has any top-layer element open that spatially overlaps it — a native <dialog> shown via .showModal(), or a popover="manual"/"auto" element shown via .showPopover() (e.g. Angular CDK in popover mode) — regardless of the overlay's own z-index. No error, no warning; it just doesn't paint.

This is the same class of bug as #39095 (ARIA snapshot UI hidden behind an Angular Material dialog), which #39123 fixed for the inspector/recorder toolbar by promoting <x-pw-glass> into the top layer via the Popover API. That fix works for the recorder because it re-promotes on a 500ms timer (packages/injected/src/recorder/recorder.ts, the recreate() loop). The screencast overlay path shares the same <x-pw-glass>/Highlight machinery but has no such loop — it promotes once, ever, and never again.

**Versions:** playwright-core@1.63.0 (stable, current npm latest) — reproduces with plain playwright, no @playwright/cli needed. Also reproduces against @playwright/cli@0.1.19's bundled 1.63.0-alpha-2026-08-31 (an older pre-release snapshot of the same line, not itself "latest").

**Root cause**

- <x-pw-glass> is promoted via popover="manual" + showPopover() — packages/injected/src/highlight.ts: _glassPaneElement.setAttribute('popover', 'manual') (~L74); install() (~L111) calls _bringToFront() (~L120), which does hidePopover(); showPopover().
- install() has exactly one call site: _ensureHighlight() in packages/injected/src/injectedScript.ts (~L1339), guarded by if (!this._highlight) — so promotion happens once, on whichever call (showOverlay, showChapter, action-annotation, screenshot masking — anything that first needs the highlight pane) creates it.
- Highlight.addUserOverlay() (highlight.ts ~L280-296), called on every showOverlay(), never re-promotes — it only appends another div.x-pw-user-overlay child and unhides the container (earlier overlay content stays in the DOM underneath later ones).
- Overlay._doAdd() (packages/playwright-core/src/server/overlay.ts) is plain server-side Node with no DOM access — it can't call hidePopover()/showPopover() itself; it just marshals html into the injected script via addUserOverlay.
- Top-layer elements paint in promotion order (last showPopover()/showModal() wins), not z-index. Once anything else on the page enters the top layer after the glass pane's one-time promotion, it permanently paints above it for the rest of that document's life.

**Minimal reproduction (no app framework needed)**

```JavaScript
await page.goto('data:text/html,' + encodeURIComponent(`
  <dialog id="d" style="position:fixed;inset:0;margin:0;width:100vw;height:100vh;padding:0;border:0;background:rgba(200,200,200,0.9)">
    dialog content
  </dialog>
  <button id="b" onclick="d.showModal()">Open</button>
`));

await page.screencast.start({ path: 'repro.webm' });
await page.screencast.showOverlay('<div style="position:absolute;top:60px;left:60px;width:200px;height:100px;background:red"></div>');
await page.screenshot({ path: '1-visible.png' });   // solid red (255,0,0)

await page.click('#b');
await page.screenshot({ path: '2-hidden.png' });    // washed-out pink (~205,180,180) — hidden under the dialog, not solid red

await page.evaluate(() => {
  const g = document.querySelector('x-pw-glass');
  if (g?.matches(':popover-open')) g.hidePopover();
  g?.showPopover();
});
await page.screenshot({ path: '3-visible-again.png' }); // solid red again

```
Identical behavior with a popover="manual" element shown via .showPopover() instead of <dialog>/showModal() — both are top-layer, and both reproduce this. showChapter() over the same dialog is 100% invisible too (every probed pixel matches the page background exactly).


**Suggested fix**
Highlight.addUserOverlay() (packages/injected/src/highlight.ts ~L293) should call this._bringToFront() on every call, not only via _ensureHighlight()'s first-call guard — mirroring what the recorder's polling loop achieves, but on-demand instead of on a timer.

**Workaround**

```JavaScript
await page.evaluate(() => {
  const g = document.querySelector('x-pw-glass');
  if (g?.matches(':popover-open')) g.hidePopover();
  g?.showPopover();
});
```
Related
#39095 / #39123 (this fix's origin — recorder-only), #36698, #28944 (same class, closed), #41504 (open, different bug on the same glass pane — backdrop tinting, not this).

### Version

0.1.19

