query:
[Bug]: Temporary iframe handles retained after frameLocator clicks

### Version

1.58.2

The same undisposed temporary handles are present in the source of `main` at `af74c938e45f3e759dc2521993f201389eb16cb6`. I have inspected that source, but have not run this reproduction against the latest release (1.63.0).

### Steps to reproduce

This is a standalone reproduction: no application framework, external website, console logging of DOM objects, or explicit `ElementHandle` created by the caller.

1. Use Node.js with Microsoft Edge installed.
2. In an empty directory, run `npm install playwright-core@1.58.2`.
3. Save the following as `repro.cjs` and run `node repro.cjs`.

```js
const { chromium } = require("playwright-core");

async function isRetained(cdp) {
  await cdp.send("HeapProfiler.collectGarbage");
  await cdp.send("HeapProfiler.collectGarbage");
  const { result } = await cdp.send("Runtime.evaluate", {
    expression: "Boolean(globalThis.iframeRef.deref())",
    returnByValue: true,
  });
  return result.value;
}

async function run(browser, mode, tracing) {
  const context = await browser.newContext();
  try {
    if (tracing)
      await context.tracing.start({ snapshots: true, screenshots: true });
    const page = await context.newPage();
    await page.setContent('<iframe srcdoc="<button>Click</button>"></iframe>');
    const button = page.frameLocator("iframe").getByRole("button");
    await button.waitFor();
    await page.evaluate(() => {
      globalThis.iframeRef = new WeakRef(document.querySelector("iframe"));
    });
    if (mode !== "no-click")
      await button.click({ force: mode === "force-click" });
    await page.evaluate(() => document.querySelector("iframe").remove());
    // Exclude Chromium's separate last-hovered-node retention.
    await page.mouse.move(500, 500);
    const cdp = await context.newCDPSession(page);
    const retained = await isRetained(cdp);
    await cdp.send("Runtime.discardConsoleEntries");
    const retainedAfterDiscard = await isRetained(cdp);
    console.log({ mode, tracing, retained, retainedAfterDiscard });
    await cdp.detach();
    if (tracing)
      await context.tracing.stop();
  } finally {
    await context.close();
  }
}

(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch({ channel: "msedge", headless: true });
  try {
    console.log({
      playwright: require("playwright-core/package.json").version,
      browser: browser.version(),
    });
    for (const tracing of [false, true]) {
      for (const mode of ["no-click", "normal-click", "force-click"])
        await run(browser, mode, tracing);
    }
  } finally {
    await browser.close();
  }
})().catch(error => {
  console.error(error);
  process.exitCode = 1;
});
```

The pointer movement is a diagnostic control, not a proposed workaround. It separates native last-hovered-node retention from the inspector-handle issue. Similarly, the forced-click case is a control, not a recommendation to disable actionability checks in tests.


### Expected behavior

After the iframe is removed, temporary handles created internally by Playwright should not prevent its collection while the page/context remains open. All six cases should print `retained: false` and `retainedAfterDiscard: false`.


### Actual behavior

For both tracing settings:

| Action | retained | retainedAfterDiscard |
| --- | --- | --- |
| No click | false | false |
| Normal click | true | true |
| Forced click | false | false |

The detached iframe's inspector retention can appear under **DevTools console** in a heap snapshot even though no DOM object was logged. Discarding console entries does not release it.


### Additional context

Instrumenting the owning Chromium protocol session identifies an unreleased `HTMLIFrameElement` remote object from `DOM.resolveNode`, acquired through:

```text
ElementHandle._checkFrameIsHitTarget
  -> frame.frameElement
  -> CRPage.getFrameElement
  -> FrameSession._adoptBackendNodeId
  -> DOM.resolveNode
```

Explicitly releasing that exact object ID on its owning session allows collection in the controlled reproduction.

There are two missing-disposal sites:

- [`ElementHandle._checkFrameIsHitTarget`](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/af74c938e45f3e759dc2521993f201389eb16cb6/packages/playwright-core/src/server/dom.ts):
  temporary ancestor iframe handles are not disposed, including early-return and exception paths. Record each handle immediately after acquisition and dispose them in `finally` after the hit-target checks.
- [`FrameSession._framePosition`](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/af74c938e45f3e759dc2521993f201389eb16cb6/packages/playwright-core/src/server/chromium/crPage.ts):
  the temporary frame element used for `boundingBox()` is not disposed. Dispose it in `finally`. This second site is identified by source inspection; the same-process `srcdoc` reproduction above directly demonstrates the first site, not independent coverage of the out-of-process frame path.

Applying these disposal changes to 1.58.2 makes all six cases print `false/false` without changing the click behavior. I have a small fix ready and would like to contribute it, with regression coverage, if maintainers approve/assign the issue as requested by CONTRIBUTING.md.


### Environment

```shell
- Windows
- Node.js 24.15.0
- Playwright core 1.58.2
- Microsoft Edge 152.0.4191.66, headless
- Tracing both enabled and disabled
```

