[Bug]: 1.63 regression - `Locator.highlight` does not work with custom selector engines that rely on global variables

### Version

1.63.0

### Steps to reproduce

```ts
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test'

declare global {
    interface Window {
        selectorEngineEnabled?: true | undefined
    }
}

export const test = base.extend<{}, { selectorRegistration: void }>({
    selectorRegistration: [
        async ({ playwright }, use) => {
            await playwright.selectors.register('tag', () => ({
                queryAll: (root: Element | Document, selector: string) => {
                    if (typeof window.selectorEngineEnabled === 'boolean') {
                        return Array.from(root.querySelectorAll(selector))
                    }
                    return []
                },
                query: (root: Element | Document, selector: string) => {
                    if (typeof window.selectorEngineEnabled === 'boolean') {
                        return root.querySelector(selector)
                    }
                    return []
                },
            }))
            await use()
        },
        { scope: 'worker', auto: true },
    ],
})

test('selector engine test', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.evaluate(() => (window.selectorEngineEnabled = true))
    await page.setContent('<button>asdf</button>')
    const button = page.locator('tag=button')
    await button.highlight() // doesn't work
    await button.click() // does work
})
```

### Expected behavior

both `button.highlight` and `button.click` should work

### Actual behavior

only `button.click` works.

it seems that `window.selectorEngineEnabled` is undefined when called by `locator.highlight`, but not when called by `locator.click`.

my guess is that maybe `locator.highlight` is incorrectly running the selector inside an isolated content script, even though the selector engine is not being registered with `{contentScript: true}`?

### Additional context

the use case is my [playwright-ui5](https://github.com/DetachHead/playwright-ui5) selector engine. it works by [accessing the ui5 api via `window.sap.ui.core`](https://github.com/DetachHead/playwright-ui5/blob/6b74925eb1f717a66c84378ccd69c1a19eaf2327/src/browser/css.ts#L65). when calling `locator.highlight` with a ui5 selector, it fails because `window.sap` is not defined for some reason.

### Environment

```shell
