[Bug]: serviceWorkers block reads serviceWorker in opaque sandboxed iframe and emits SecurityError

### Problem

With `serviceWorkers: "block"`, Playwright injects a script that reads `navigator.serviceWorker` in every frame. In a `sandbox="allow-scripts"` iframe (opaque origin), Chromium throws a SecurityError at the getter. This emits a pageerror before any application code needs service workers.

Reproduced on @playwright/test 1.63.0 and 1.64.0-alpha-2026-10-04, each using its matching Chromium. A route-fulfilled localhost document is sufficient: no server, app, authentication, or network service is required.

### Minimal reproduction

```js
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { chromium } from '@playwright/test';
const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true });
try {
  const context = await browser.newContext({ serviceWorkers: 'block' });
  try {
    const page = await context.newPage();
    const errors = [];
    page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(error.message));
    await page.route('http://127.0.0.1:8123/', route => route.fulfill({
      contentType: 'text/html',
      body: '<iframe sandbox="allow-scripts" srcdoc="<p>Export preview</p>"></iframe>'
    }));
    await page.goto('http://127.0.0.1:8123/');
    await page.frameLocator('iframe').locator('p').waitFor();
    assert.equal(await page.locator('iframe').getAttribute('sandbox'), 'allow-scripts');
    assert.deepEqual(errors, []); // fails: serviceWorker getter SecurityError
  } finally { await context.close(); }
} finally { await browser.close(); }
```

Actual error mentions: Failed to read the 'serviceWorker' property, and missing 'allow-same-origin'.

Expected: no pageerror from the blocking init script for an opaque origin where service workers are already unavailable. Registration must remain blocked in eligible frames. The iframe sandbox must remain unchanged.

### Proposed owner-level fix

Guard the navigator.serviceWorker accessor in BrowserContext initialization. If that accessor throws SecurityError, skip service-worker setup for that document. Re-throw other exceptions; preserve the existing register-blocking implementation for origins that expose serviceWorker. This avoids changes to application sandbox policy or test pageerror handling.

