I'd like to take this. Root cause is in packages/playwright-core/src/server/fetch.ts ( etch): the object form merges into the existing query —

`	s
const requestUrl = new URL(constructURLBasedOnBaseURL(defaults.baseURL, params.url));
if (params.encodedParams) {
  requestUrl.search = params.encodedParams;        // replaces the whole query
} else if (params.params) {
  for (const { name, value } of params.params)
    requestUrl.searchParams.append(name, value);   // merges, as expected
}
`

When params is a string or URLSearchParams the client sets encodedParams (client/fetch.ts:205-209), and assigning .search discards the query already present in the URL (e.g. page=2). That is why only the object form keeps the existing params.

Fix: append the encoded params through searchParams instead of overwriting .search — parse 
ew URLSearchParams(params.encodedParams) and ^Gppend each pair — so all three forms merge identically. I'll add a regression test in the APIRequestContext request suite covering string and URLSearchParams params against a URL that already has a query, and open a PR once a maintainer confirms the direction.

