[Bug]: [MCP/CLI] Bare loopback IP addresses (127.0.0.1:port) and hosts with ports fail to navigate due to erroneous scheme inference

### What's going on?

In Playwright CLI and MCP server (`playwright open`, `tab-new`, `browser_navigate`), when opening or navigating to URLs specified without an explicit scheme:

1. **Bare loopback IP addresses fail with `net::ERR_SSL_PROTOCOL_ERROR`:**
   When targeting local development servers on loopback IPs (e.g., `127.0.0.1:3000`, `0.0.0.0:8000`, `[::1]:8080`), navigation fails immediately:
   ```text
   page.goto: net::ERR_SSL_PROTOCOL_ERROR at https://127.0.0.1:3000/
   ```
   This happens because `checkUrlAndNavigate` only checks `url.startsWith('localhost')` before defaulting to `https://`. As local development servers predominantly run on plain HTTP, forcing `https://` causes SSL protocol failure.

2. **Bare hostnames with ports fail with `net::ERR_ABORTED`:**
   When specifying a bare host with a port (e.g., `example.com:8080`), navigation fails:
   ```text
   page.goto: net::ERR_ABORTED at example.com:8080
   ```
   According to the WHATWG URL standard, `new URL('example.com:8080')` parses successfully with `protocol: "example.com:"` and `pathname: "8080"`. Because `new URL(...)` does not throw an error, the `try / catch` block in `checkUrlAndNavigate` is bypassed entirely, leaving the raw string without an `http://` or `https://` scheme.

### Visual Evidence

**1. Reproduction — SSL Protocol Error on Loopback IP & Aborted Custom Scheme:**
![MCP Bare URL Reproduction](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alok-108/assets/main/mcp_bare_url_repro.png)

**2. Fixed Behavior — Loopback IPs and Ported Hosts Normalized Properly:**
![MCP Bare URL Fixed](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alok-108/assets/main/mcp_bare_url_fixed.png)

### Why does this happen?

In `packages/playwright-core/src/tools/backend/tab.ts`:

```ts
async checkUrlAndNavigate(url: string): Promise<string> {
  try {
    new URL(url);
  } catch (e) {
    if (url.startsWith('localhost'))
      url = 'http://' + url;
    else
      url = 'https://' + url;
  }
  this.context.checkUrlAllowed(url);
  await this.navigate(url);
  return url;
}
```

- WHATWG `new URL()` does not throw on `host:port` because `host:` is treated as a valid scheme name if `host` begins with an ASCII alpha character (`[a-zA-Z]`).
- Loopback IPs begin with numbers (`127.0.0.1`) so `new URL()` throws, but the catch branch only checks `localhost`, falling through to `https://` for all IPv4/IPv6 loopback addresses.

### Expected behavior

1. URLs without an explicit scheme (`^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\/\/` or `^(about|data|blob|javascript):`) should be normalized.
2. Local loopback addresses (`localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `0.0.0.0`, `[::1]`) should default to `http://`.
3. Other bare hosts (e.g. `example.com:8080`, `playwright.dev`) should default to `https://`.

