query:
[MCP]: browser_cookie_set fails with internal assertion error when domain is omitted on blank page

### What's going on?

Following up on closed issue #43274 to isolate individual reproducible cases. This report covers the error handling when invoking `browser_cookie_set` on a blank tab (`about:blank`) without an explicit `domain`.

When an agent or user invokes `browser_cookie_set` immediately after opening a browser or on an unnavigated tab (`about:blank`):
```json
{
  "name": "browser_cookie_set",
  "arguments": {
    "name": "session_id",
    "value": "xyz123"
  }
}
```

In `packages/playwright-core/src/tools/backend/cookies.ts` (lines 103–109):
```ts
const url = new URL(tab.page.url());
const cookie: any = {
  name: params.name,
  value: params.value,
  domain: params.domain || url.hostname,
  path: params.path || '/',
};
```

On `about:blank`, `new URL('about:blank').hostname` is `""`. When `params.domain` is omitted, `cookie.domain` becomes `""`.
When passed to `browserContext.addCookies([cookie])`, Playwright's internal validation in `packages/playwright-core/src/server/network.ts` line 165 checks:
```ts
assert(c.url || (c.domain && c.path), 'Cookie should have a url or a domain/path pair');
```
Because `c.domain === ""`, `(c.domain && c.path)` evaluates to `""` (falsy), and Playwright throws an internal assertion failure:
```text
Error: browserBackend.callTool: Cookie should have a url or a domain/path pair
```

### Reproduction

![MCP Cookie Set about:blank Repro](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alok-108/assets/main/mcp_cookie_set_about_blank_repro.png)

```ts
test('browser_cookie_set on about:blank without domain', async ({ startClient }) => {
  const { client } = await startClient({ config: { capabilities: ['storage'] } });

  const response = await client.callTool({
    name: 'browser_cookie_set',
    arguments: { name: 'session_id', value: 'xyz123' },
  });

  // Fails with: Error: browserBackend.callTool: Cookie should have a url or a domain/path pair
});
```

### Expected Behavior
Rather than crashing with an internal core assertion error (`Cookie should have a url or a domain/path pair`), `browser_cookie_set` should validate that the domain can be determined and report an actionable error to the client/LLM:
```text
Cannot infer cookie domain from current page URL "about:blank". Please specify "domain".
```

### Version
Playwright main / 1.65.0-next

