query:
[Bug]: run-server retains closed Browser objects in _dontReuseBrowsers

### Version

1.64.1 (npm `latest` when tested). The same registration is present in [`main` at 5ad202df4f48](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/5ad202df4f484d593ab42a4a16e6c75f666fef38/packages/playwright-core/src/remote/playwrightServer.ts#L282-L318); I have not run the reproduction against `main`.

### Steps to reproduce

A long-lived `run-server` retains each Browser it launches after that browser has closed. This also happens when the client process disconnects abruptly. No external application or website is involved.

Save the reproduction files included below in one directory, then run:

```sh
npm install playwright-core@1.64.1
npx playwright-core install --with-deps chromium
node repro.cjs
```

The script starts the standard `playwright-core/cli.js run-server` CLI on loopback and an ephemeral port. It performs 20 `chromium.connect()` / screenshot / `browser.close()` cycles, followed by 20 additional cycles where the client process is killed after its screenshot. Each screenshot is checked for a PNG signature.

For observation only, a preload wraps `_initLaunchBrowserMode` to save **WeakRefs** and samples `_dontReuseBrowsers`, the active browser registry, and those WeakRefs after two GC passes in separate asynchronous jobs. It does not change browser launch or cleanup behavior.

Complete runnable reproduction, one-line bundle patch, Docker commands and raw results are included below, so the report is self-contained.

The public API trigger in the normal-close scenario is:

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
  const browser = await chromium.connect(endpoint);
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.setContent('<h1>Standalone retention reproduction</h1>');
  await page.screenshot();
  await browser.close();
}
```


### Expected behavior

Once the connection/browser is closed and server-side cleanup has finished, the closed Browser should no longer be held in `_dontReuseBrowsers` and should become eligible for garbage collection.

### Actual behavior

All 40 PNG screenshots succeed. The active browser registry is empty after each batch, but both `_dontReuseBrowsers.size` and the count of reachable Browser WeakRefs grow with the completed connections:

| Completed connections | Last batch | Active browsers | Set size / reachable Browser objects |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | Baseline | 0 | 0 / 0 |
| 10 | Normal close | 0 | 10 / 10 |
| 20 | Normal close | 0 | 20 / 20 |
| 30 | Client process killed | 0 | 30 / 30 |
| 40 | Client process killed | 0 | 40 / 40 |

This reports object retention, not a claim of linear RSS growth.

### Additional context / proposed fix

`_initLaunchBrowserMode` registers the Browser directly in the Set:

```diff
- this._dontReuseBrowsers.add(browser);
+ this._dontReuse(browser);
```

The existing `_dontReuse()` helper already installs a `Browser.Events.Disconnected` listener that removes the Browser from the Set. Replacing only this registration in the installed 1.64.1 bundle makes **all checkpoints above return Set size 0 and reachable Browser objects 0**, for both normal close and terminated clients, while all 40 screenshots still succeed.

The reproduction includes `patch.cjs`, which verifies there is exactly one matching launch registration in the 1.64.1 bundle before replacing it. Run `node patch.cjs` followed by `EXPECT_FIXED=1 node repro.cjs`; the latter exits unsuccessfully if any closed Browser remains retained at a checkpoint.

I would be happy to contribute the one-line source fix and a regression test if maintainers approve that approach.

### Environment

- Official Docker image: `mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.64.1-noble`
- OS: Ubuntu 24.04, Linux ARM64
- Node.js: v24.21.0
- npm dependency: `playwright-core@1.64.1`
- Browser: bundled Chromium, default headless mode
- Reproduction containers had no external network access; only loopback was used.

<details>
<summary>repro.cjs</summary>

```js
'use strict';
// Run: node repro.cjs (after npm install playwright-core@1.64.1).
// The trigger uses the public connect/page/close API and the unmodified run-server CLI.
// The preload observes server-side object lifetime; it does not retain Browser objects.
const path = require('node:path');
const {spawn} = require('node:child_process');
const packageRoot = path.dirname(require.resolve('playwright-core/package.json'));
const delay = ms => new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, ms));

if (process.env.REPRO_OBSERVER === '1') {
  const {remote: {PlaywrightServer}} = require(path.join(packageRoot, 'lib/coreBundle.js'));
  const proto = PlaywrightServer.prototype;
  const original = proto._initLaunchBrowserMode;
  const refs = [];
  let server;
  proto._initLaunchBrowserMode = async function(...args) {
    server = this;
    const result = await original.apply(this, args);
    refs.push(new WeakRef(result.preLaunchedBrowser));
    return result;
  };
  process.on('message', async message => {
    if (message.type !== 'snapshot') return;
    // Yield between GC passes; WeakRef targets remain live until the current job ends.
    await delay(100);
    global.gc();
    await delay(100);
    global.gc();
    process.send({type: 'snapshot', id: message.id,
      retainedSet: server?._dontReuseBrowsers.size ?? 0,
      liveBrowsers: server?._playwright.allBrowsers().length ?? 0,
      reachableBrowserObjects: refs.filter(ref => ref.deref()).length,
      heapUsed: process.memoryUsage().heapUsed});
  });
} else if (process.env.REPRO_CLIENT === '1') {
  (async () => {
    const {chromium} = require('playwright-core');
    const browser = await chromium.connect(process.env.REPRO_ENDPOINT);
    const page = await browser.newPage();
    await page.setContent('<h1>Standalone retention reproduction</h1>');
    const screenshot = await page.screenshot();
    if (!screenshot.subarray(0, 8).equals(Buffer.from('89504e470d0a1a0a', 'hex')))
      throw new Error('Not a PNG');
    process.send({type: 'rendered'});
    // The parent kills this client to simulate an abruptly disconnected consumer.
  })().catch(error => {console.error(error); process.exit(1);});
} else {
  (async () => {
    const {chromium} = require('playwright-core');
    const server = spawn(process.execPath, ['--expose-gc', '--require', __filename,
      path.join(packageRoot, 'cli.js'), 'run-server', '--host', '127.0.0.1', '--port', '0'], {
      env: {...process.env, REPRO_OBSERVER: '1'}, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe', 'ipc']});
    let stderr = '';
    server.stderr.on('data', data => stderr += data);
    const deadline = setTimeout(() => {server.kill('SIGKILL'); console.error('Reproduction timeout'); process.exit(1);}, 180000);
    const results = {version: require('playwright-core/package.json').version,
      node: process.version, platform: process.platform, arch: process.arch, samples: []};
    let id = 0;
    const snapshot = async (phase, completed) => {
      const requestId = ++id;
      const reply = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        const timer = setTimeout(() => {server.off('message', handler); reject(new Error('Snapshot timeout'));}, 10000);
        function handler(message) {
          if (message.type !== 'snapshot' || message.id !== requestId) return;
          clearTimeout(timer); server.off('message', handler); resolve(message);
        }
        server.on('message', handler);
      });
      server.send({type: 'snapshot', id: requestId});
      const {type, id: ignored, ...sample} = await reply;
      results.samples.push({phase, completed, ...sample});
      if (sample.liveBrowsers !== 0) throw new Error('Browser cleanup not finished');
    };
    try {
      const endpoint = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        let stdout = '';
        server.stdout.on('data', data => {
          stdout += data;
          const match = stdout.match(/Listening on (ws:\/\/[^\s]+)/);
          if (match) resolve(match[1]);
        });
        server.once('exit', code => reject(new Error(`Server exited ${code}: ${stderr}`)));
      });
      await snapshot('baseline', 0);
      for (let i = 1; i <= 20; i++) {
        const browser = await chromium.connect(endpoint);
        const page = await browser.newPage();
        await page.setContent('<h1>Standalone retention reproduction</h1>');
        const png = await page.screenshot();
        if (!png.subarray(0, 8).equals(Buffer.from('89504e470d0a1a0a', 'hex'))) throw new Error('Not a PNG');
        await browser.close();
        if (i % 10 === 0) await snapshot('normal-close', i);
      }
      for (let i = 1; i <= 20; i++) {
        const client = spawn(process.execPath, [__filename], {
          env: {...process.env, REPRO_CLIENT: '1', REPRO_ENDPOINT: endpoint},
          stdio: ['ignore', 'ignore', 'inherit', 'ipc']});
        await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
          client.once('message', message => message.type === 'rendered' ? resolve() : reject(new Error('Unexpected client message')));
          client.once('exit', code => reject(new Error(`Client exited before render: ${code}`)));
        });
        await new Promise(resolve => {client.once('exit', resolve); client.kill('SIGKILL');});
        await delay(200);
        if (i % 10 === 0) await snapshot('client-killed', 20 + i);
      }
      console.log(JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));
      if (process.env.EXPECT_FIXED === '1' && results.samples.some(s => s.retainedSet || s.reachableBrowserObjects))
        throw new Error('Closed Browser objects are retained');
    } finally {
      clearTimeout(deadline);
      server.kill('SIGTERM');
      await new Promise(resolve => {server.once('exit', resolve); setTimeout(() => {server.kill('SIGKILL'); resolve();}, 5000).unref();});
    }
  })().catch(error => {console.error(error); process.exitCode = 1;});
}
