````markdown
# Playwright run-server closed Browser retention

Standalone reproduction for `playwright-core@1.64.1`. No application server or external page is needed. The only npm dependency is the public Playwright package.

## Run with the official image

From this directory:

```sh
docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/repro" -w /repro mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.64.1-noble npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund

docker run --rm --init --network none --shm-size 1g -v "$PWD:/repro" -w /repro mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.64.1-noble node repro.cjs

docker run --rm --network none -v "$PWD:/repro" -w /repro mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.64.1-noble node patch.cjs

docker run --rm --init --network none --shm-size 1g -e EXPECT_FIXED=1 -v "$PWD:/repro" -w /repro mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.64.1-noble node repro.cjs
```

`npm ci` restores the unpatched package when repeating the experiment. Alternatively, on Linux with Node 20+ and Chromium's system dependencies installed, use `npm ci`, `npx playwright-core install chromium`, and `node repro.cjs` directly.

## What it does

The script starts the standard `playwright-core/cli.js run-server` CLI. It connects with the public `chromium.connect()` API, creates a page with static content, verifies a PNG screenshot, then calls `browser.close()`, twenty times. It then repeats twenty times with separate client processes terminated using SIGKILL after a successful screenshot.

A test-only preload wraps `_initLaunchBrowserMode` to retain WeakRefs, not strong references, to the launched Browser objects. It samples the server's existing Set and active browser registry after two GC passes separated by asynchronous jobs. The preload does not change launch or cleanup behavior. The patched run changes just the launch registration from `_dontReuseBrowsers.add(browser)` to `_dontReuse(browser)` in the installed npm bundle.

## Observed result

Official `mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.64.1-noble`, Linux ARM64, Node v24.21.0. Every screenshot succeeded. `liveBrowsers` is zero at every checkpoint.

| Completed cycles | Scenario | Unpatched Set / reachable Browser objects | Patched Set / reachable Browser objects |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | Baseline | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |
| 10 | Normal close | 10 / 10 | 0 / 0 |
| 20 | Normal close | 20 / 20 | 0 / 0 |
| 30 | 10 additional killed clients | 30 / 30 | 0 / 0 |
| 40 | 20 additional killed clients | 40 / 40 | 0 / 0 |

Raw output is in `unpatched.json` and `patched.json`. This establishes retained closed objects; it does not claim linear RSS growth or characterize every remote-server mode.
````

