query:
[Feature]: Allow `retryStrategy: 'isolated'` in test.describe.configure() for tests requiring zero background workers

### 🚀 Feature Request

Playwright recently introduced retryStrategy: 'isolated', however, it is currently restricted to the global testConfig. It'd be very helpful if retryStrategy was implemented at the test file level in test.describe.configure() so isolated retries can be targeted only to tests that require zero concurrency to pass.


### Existing features do not solve this
1. Why `lock` doesn't work:
lock is an opt-in named mutex, not a runner-wide exclusive lock:
If Test A has { lock: 'foo' }, it only blocks other tests that also declare { lock: 'foo' }.
All other unlocked tests in the repository still run concurrently in background workers alongside Test A.
To achieve true isolation with lock, we would have to add { lock: 'foo' } to every single test in the entire codebase, which would completely eliminate parallel execution for the whole test run.
2. Why global retryStrategy: 'isolated' in playwright.config.ts is insufficient:
It is currently an all-or-nothing global flag.
It forces every failed test across thousands of unrelated files to defer its retries to the single-worker tail phase, even if 99% of tests are completely stateless and should just retry immediately.

### Example

```
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

// Only this suite will be retried in isolation if concurrency causes a failure
test.describe.configure({
  retries: 1,
  retryStrategy: 'isolated',
 });

test.describe('tests that fail under concurrent execution', () => {
  test('exclusive test', async ({ page }) => {
    /* Runs in parallel initially.
    If it collides with another worker and fails, it is retried
    at the end of the run with no other tests running concurrently. */
  });
});
```
Expected Behaviour:

Global/default retry strategy remains 'immediate' (or whatever is set in playwright.config.ts).
Test files configured with override, retryStrategy: 'isolated' at the test.describe level are queued to run in isolation (one worker, no other concurrent tests running) upon failure.

### Motivation

We have specific tests that require zero-concurrency isolation (meaning no other worker threads can be running anywhere in the runner at the same time) to pass as the nature of these tests make them extremely vulnerable to cross-test interference. We want our test suite to run in parallel by default but if these specific tests fail under concurrency, we want their retries to run in isolation without background workers.

