query:
[Bug]: Chromium – locale is not applied to Accept-Language / navigator.languages inside dedicated Workers

### Version

1.64.1

### Steps to reproduce

(versions reproduced: 1.59.1 and 1.64.1)
Save as `repro.js`, run `npm i playwright && npx playwright install chromium && node repro.js`.

```js
const http = require('http');
const { chromium } = require('playwright');

const seen = [];
const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
  seen.push(`${req.url.padEnd(40)} Accept-Language: ${req.headers['accept-language']}`);
  if (req.url === '/') {
    res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html' });
    return res.end(`<script>
      fetch('/from-page?languages=' + navigator.languages);
      new Worker('/worker.js');
    </script>`);
  }
  if (req.url === '/worker.js') {
    res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/javascript' });
    return res.end(`fetch('/from-worker?languages=' + navigator.languages);`);
  }
  res.end('ok');
});

(async () => {
  await new Promise(r => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', r));
  const browser = await chromium.launch();
  const context = await browser.newContext({ locale: 'de-DE' });
  const page = await context.newPage();
  await page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}/`);
  await page.waitForTimeout(1000);
  console.log(`Chromium ${browser.version()}`);
  console.log(seen.filter(line => !line.startsWith('/favicon')).join('\n'));
  await browser.close();
  server.close();
})();
```

### Expected behavior

Requests made from inside the Worker send `Accept-Language: de-DE`, and `navigator.languages` inside the Worker is `de-DE`, matching the page.

### Actual behavior

```
Chromium 147.0.7727.15
/                                        Accept-Language: de-DE
/from-page?languages=de-DE               Accept-Language: de-DE
/worker.js                               Accept-Language: de-DE
/from-worker?languages=en-US             Accept-Language: en-US,en;q=0.9
```
The Worker's own `fetch` uses the browser default Accept-Language, and its `navigator.languages` ignores `locale`.

### Additional context

`userAgent` is propagated to dedicated Workers, but `locale` is not. In `crPage.ts` (`FrameSession._onAttachedToTarget`), the `worker` branch doesn't call `setUserAgentOverride` with `acceptLanguage`. Sending `Emulation.setUserAgentOverride({ userAgent, acceptLanguage: 'de-DE' })` on the worker's CDP session fixes both the header and `navigator.languages`, similar to what #41071 did for service workers. Related: #38919 (Firefox, fixed), #13919.

### Environment

```shell
System:
    OS: macOS 26.7.1
    CPU: (14) arm64 Apple M4 Pro
    Memory: 3.03 GB / 48.00 GB
  Binaries:
    Node: 24.15.0 - ~/.volta/tools/image/node/24.15.0/bin/node
    npm: 11.12.1 - ~/.volta/tools/image/npm/11.12.1/bin/npm
    bun: 1.3.1 - ~/.bun/bin/bun
  IDEs:
    VSCode: 1.142.0 - /usr/local/bin/code
  Languages:
    Bash: 5.3.3 - /opt/homebrew/bin/bash
  npmPackages:
    playwright: 1.59.1 => 1.59.1
```

